WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:14.400
Amen. Well, thank you for that nice introduction, Pastor Pete, and it is nice for me and my family to be visiting Ann Arbor.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:24.400
This time around, like Pastor Pete mentioned, we lived here for a long time. My wife and I, and it's nice to see some old friends here.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:30.400
It's nice to see some new friends here as well as get to spend this Sunday with you all.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.880
We definitely appreciate the longstanding friendship

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.840
that we've had, but also the partnership in God's mission

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.840
as we try to bring the gospel to the nations of the world.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.800
And so you have all been a part of that through your prayers,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.000
through the church's support, through some of you

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.720
who are personal partners as well.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.480
And so we're just grateful to be here with you.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.000
We're grateful for you.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.880
And I hope that this time in God's word

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.760
ministers to you as well this morning.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.080
We're going to be looking at Psalm 126.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.720
And the title of my sermon today is called Joy

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.080
along the journey.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.520
Joy along the journey.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.160
This sermon is a personally written

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.200
exposition of Psalm 126.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.680
But it is influenced heavily by a chapter

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.920
in Eugene Peterson's book Along Obedience in the same direction.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.840
So this chapter is a meditation on some,

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.280
the chapter that I'm referring to is a meditation

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:39.360
on Psalm 126 and God really used Peterson

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.880
and this particular chapter to minister to me a lot

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.480
in this season of my life.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.560
And so I didn't copy any of his work directly,

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.040
but I did recall a lot from memory

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.520
as I was writing the sermon.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.840
And so I just wanted to let you know that up front, okay?

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.200
One thing that Eugene Peterson points out very keenly

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.240
is how we in our current world

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.520
use our modern day entertainment to numb ourselves

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.320
from various trials and sorrows that we face in life,

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.080
difficulties that we face in life.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.600
And so we will pay money to watch a comedy movie

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:26.040
or we'll pay money to watch a stand-up comedian perform and just give us

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:32.560
one or two hours of just some time to laugh and time to forget about what's

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.800
going on in in our lives or we'll scroll we'll scroll on social media to find

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:43.560
silly short-form videos that will make us laugh hysterically that we might

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.560
want to share with our friends or our family members to make them laugh as

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:56.120
well, but what I would say is that these diversions hardly give us joy. And the joy that I'm talking about

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:04.360
is this lightness of heart despite whatever challenging situations that we face. And I don't mean to

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:10.680
like poo poo on these things. They're not all bad things. They can be good legitimate forms of

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:17.480
recreation when watched in moderation and with discernment. And that's something that I am constantly

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:23.240
trying to assess of growth, the process of character building, the process of

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:30.200
sanctifying that I can testify, have ended in joy in many ways. And in the ways

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:38.640
that it hasn't yet produced joy, I'm trusting that God will end it in joy as

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:45.480
well. And I hope that you too can exercise faith in your life journey because we

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:53.190
know from scripture that God turns our sorrows into joy. So let's pray and I'll close this time

00:03:53.190 --> 00:04:08.020
in God's word. God, thank you so much for your word. Forgive us for taking it for granted, but

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:19.460
thank you that you feed us through all these recollections of how you have interceded in history

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:36.060
for people that are broken, messed up, failures, wounded, and we can definitely connect with

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:39.320
that God here.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:48.040
But we also thank you that we can exercise our faith in Christ who, for the joy, set

00:04:48.040 --> 00:05:00.030
for him endured the cross to redeem us ultimately to bring glory to you and so

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:10.630
God we ask and we pray and bring you our sorrows our hardships our pains our

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:23.120
failures we trust you not to make them go away but that you are somehow

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:30.800
working for our good and for your glory to sanctify us, to build us up, to prepare

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:37.340
us. And I pray that that would be the posture of each person here before you

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:42.020
today. I love you, thank you, Jesus' name, amen.
